From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Lemire <daniel@lemire.me>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:11:53 -0400
Subject: src: stop including simdjson.h from env.h

Backport of https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/66620 (upstream commit
https://github.com/nodejs/node/commit/2b17b43eeba4484d43afaa1d5e3f951f006c5df6).
Only the include-reduction commit is taken; the simdjson 5.0.3 update
from the same PR is not.

env.h includes inspector_profiler.h, which included simdjson.h for
the types of two virtual methods and a parser member. As a result,
about 155 files in src/ parsed the amalgamated simdjson header, which
is over 10 MB.

Keep simdjson out of inspector_profiler.h: the profile connections
now say which field of `result` holds the profile, and
WriteProfile() takes the profile as raw JSON. The parser becomes a
local variable, so its buffers are no longer kept alive for the
lifetime of the Environment. Also drop the unused include from
node_task_runner.h.

The upstream change to src/node_config_file.cc is omitted: it removes
a second parse of the config file that does not exist on v24.x.

This patch can be removed when Electron updates to a Node.js release
that contains nodejs/node#66620.

